/**
 * @defgroup Foundation_Workflows_ReleaseV1 Foundation 1.x Stabilization Backlog
 * @ingroup Foundation_Workflows_Validation
 * @brief Version-controlled plan and quality gates for the Foundation 1.x line.
 *
 * This page is the source of truth for Foundation 1.x stabilization. Update it
 * in the same commit that changes a task's status or acceptance evidence. Do
 * not maintain a separate progress copy in chat, a spreadsheet, or a Gantt.
 *
 * @section FoundationReleaseV1Status Status Header
 *
 * | Field | Value |
 * | ----- | ----- |
 * | Current release | `v1.2.0` |
 * | Working branch | `main` (trunk-based development) |
 * | Overall status | `IN PROGRESS` |
 * | Current milestone | M3 - Test depth and code quality |
 * | Last reviewed | 2026-09-25 |
 * | Release state | `v1.2.0` published; stabilization continues |
 *
 * Allowed task states are:
 *
 * | State | Meaning |
 * | ----- | ------- |
 * | `NEXT` | The next task to execute. |
 * | `TODO` | Accepted scope, not started. |
 * | `IN PROGRESS` | Work exists locally or on a branch but is not accepted. |
 * | `BLOCKED` | Cannot continue until the recorded dependency is resolved. |
 * | `DONE` | Acceptance criteria passed and evidence is recorded. |
 * | `DEFERRED` | Explicitly removed from the current 1.x scope. |
 *
 * @section FoundationReleaseV1Rules Update Rules
 *
 * - Keep task IDs stable so commits and conversations can refer to them.
 * - Change a task to `DONE` only after all stated acceptance criteria pass.
 * - Record evidence as a commit SHA, CI run, command log, package inspection,
 *   consumer build, or hardware-validation record.
 * - A successful cross-compilation is not evidence of target execution.
 * - A test run that discovers zero tests is not a passing test result.
 * - When scope changes, mark the task `DEFERRED` and explain why; do not delete it.
 * - Update the status header and release gates whenever this backlog changes.
 *
 * @section FoundationReleaseV1Roadmap Dependency Roadmap
 *
 * This dependency roadmap is intentionally used instead of a dated Gantt. Add
 * calendar dates only after runner and hardware availability is known.
 *
 * @dot
 * digraph FoundationReleaseV1Roadmap {
 *     rankdir=TB;
 *     graph [
 *         bgcolor="transparent",
 *         pad="0.25",
 *         nodesep="0.55",
 *         ranksep="0.65"
 *     ];
 *     node [
 *         shape=box,
 *         style="rounded,filled",
 *         color="#34495e",
 *         fontcolor="#17202a",
 *         fontname="Helvetica",
 *         fontsize=11,
 *         margin="0.18,0.12"
 *     ];
 *     edge [
 *         color="#5d6d7e",
 *         penwidth=1.5,
 *         arrowsize=0.8
 *     ];
 *
 *     M1 [label="M1\nRelease contract", fillcolor="#d6eaf8"];
 *     M2 [label="M2\nContinuous integration", fillcolor="#d6eaf8"];
 *     M3 [label="M3\nTest depth and code quality", fillcolor="#fcf3cf"];
 *     M4 [label="M4\nPackage and workflow hardening", fillcolor="#fcf3cf"];
 *     M5 [label="M5\nPlatform and hardware validation", fillcolor="#fadbd8"];
 *     M6 [label="M6\nSustained 1.x releases", fillcolor="#d5f5e3"];
 *
 *     M1 -> M2;
 *     M2 -> M3;
 *     M2 -> M4;
 *     M3 -> M5;
 *     M4 -> M5;
 *     M5 -> M6;
 *
 *     { rank=same; M3; M4; }
 * }
 * @enddot
 *
 * @section FoundationReleaseV1Baseline Completed Baseline
 *
 * | ID | State | Deliverable | Evidence |
 * | -- | ----- | ----------- | -------- |
 * | BASE-001 | `DONE` | Pre-v1 scripts, presets, toolchains, and workflow baseline | `943c192` |
 * | BASE-002 | `DONE` | Modular GoogleTests and cross-platform example layout | `33ca3c7` |
 * | BASE-003 | `DONE` | Release-only exported packages | `96c0892` |
 * | BASE-004 | `DONE` | Auto-discovered interactive example launchers | `f2786cc` |
 *
 * @section FoundationReleaseV1M1 M1 - Release Contract
 *
 * | ID | Priority | State | Task | Acceptance criteria / evidence |
 * | -- | -------- | ----- | ---- | ------------------------------ |
 * | V1-001 | P0 | `DONE` | Define the support matrix | Every public preset is classified in @ref Foundation_BuildGuide_SupportMatrix; PIC is deferred and unvalidated candidates cannot be called supported. |
 * | V1-002 | P0 | `DONE` | Make version and language requirements consistent | CMake, `library.properties`, source mode, README, and Doxygen report 1.2.0 and C++17; CMake rejects version drift; direct source mode rejects C++14; clean macOS Arm64 Debug and Release runs each pass 122 tests. |
 * | V1-003 | P0 | `BLOCKED` | Confirm the distribution license | Interim state is `All Rights Reserved / No License Granted`; publishing artifacts grants no external-use rights. @ref Foundation_Workflows_LegalReview records current guardrails, known repository facts, counsel questions, the evidence-packet checklist, and objective exit criteria. Only qualified legal review can close the task. |
 * | V1-004 | P0 | `DONE` | Audit and freeze the public API | All 16 findings have documented dispositions; native CI and the isolated exported-package consumer validate `Foundation::Foundation`. See @ref Foundation_Workflows_PublicApiAudit. |
 * | V1-005 | P1 | `DONE` | Maintain release history and limitations | `CHANGELOG.md` records 1.1.0 as the first published release, 1.2.0 as current, and 1.0.0 as superseded; @ref Foundation_BuildGuide_KnownLimitations records remaining boundaries. |
 *
 * M1 exits when the public contract no longer contradicts the build and every
 * advertised platform has an explicit support level.
 *
 * @section FoundationReleaseV1M2 M2 - Continuous Integration
 *
 * | ID | Priority | State | Task | Acceptance criteria / evidence |
 * | -- | -------- | ----- | ---- | ------------------------------ |
 * | CI-001 | P0 | `DONE` | Add native build and test CI | [Run 36194411008](https://github.com/ChecheRomo96/Foundation/actions/runs/36194411008) passed the current Debug and Release suite on macOS/Apple Clang, Linux/GCC, Linux/Clang, Windows/MSVC, and Windows/Clang for `v1.2.0`. |
 * | CI-002 | P0 | `DONE` | Validate exported packages in CI | The same run completed fresh Release exports and successfully linked and executed the standalone `Foundation::Foundation` consumer in all five native jobs. |
 * | CI-003 | P1 | `IN PROGRESS` | Validate documentation on pull requests | `.github/workflows/deploy-docs.yml` now performs a fresh warning-as-error Doxygen build on pull requests with read-only permission and keeps deployment in a separate push-only job. Local YAML parsing and Doxygen generation pass; the first hosted run remains to be recorded. |
 * | CI-004 | P1 | `IN PROGRESS` | Add embedded compile jobs | `.github/workflows/embedded-ci.yml` builds Debug/Release, exports Release, verifies target object identity and package policy, and uploads all AVR, generic Arm, PSoC, and STM32 packages without pretending to execute target code. AVR passed the equivalent local sequence. The local Arm compiler lacks Newlib; CI installs it explicitly. The first hosted run remains to be recorded. |
 * | CI-005 | P1 | `TODO` | Preserve useful failure evidence | CI uploads logs, test reports, and selected package artifacts needed to reproduce a failure. |
 *
 * Docker may support Linux and cross-compiler jobs. It does not replace native
 * Windows/MSVC or macOS runners.
 *
 * @section FoundationReleaseV1M3 M3 - Test Depth and Code Quality
 *
 * | ID | Priority | State | Task | Acceptance criteria / evidence |
 * | -- | -------- | ----- | ---- | ------------------------------ |
 * | TEST-001 | P0 | `DONE` | Inventory public API coverage | @ref Foundation_Workflows_PublicApiCoverage maps every public family to behavior, conformance, compile, configuration, consumer, or target evidence. The behavior gaps assigned to `TEST-002` and `TEST-003` and the header gap assigned to `TEST-004` are closed. |
 * | TEST-002 | P0 | `DONE` | Complete Math tests | 23 focused cases now cover Complex, fixed/dynamic matrix member APIs, arithmetic, trigonometry, Ratio mutators, and numeric edges. Clean macOS Arm64 Debug and Release runs each pass all 145/145 registered tests. Matrix multiplication already covers all four fixed/dynamic operand combinations plus incompatible, attached-output, and overlap paths. |
 * | TEST-003 | P0 | `DONE` | Complete remaining module tests | Sixteen focused cases close every inventoried Containers, Functional, Time, Scheduling, and Utils behavior gap; TypeTraits was already complete through its shared standard/fallback conformance suite. Clean macOS Arm64 Debug and Release runs each pass all 161/161 registered tests. |
 * | TEST-004 | P1 | `DONE` | Add public-header self-containment checks | `tests/CMakeLists.txt` generates one translation unit per staged `.h` (each included twice to also check its guard) into `FoundationHeaderSelfContainment`, exposed as the `FoundationHeaders.SelfContained` CTest case. Only headers of enabled features are checked. The default macOS Arm64 build checks all 57 headers; Debug and Release each pass 162/162 tests. |
 * | TEST-005 | P1 | `DONE` | Add warning and sanitizer jobs | Supported native compilers run an agreed warning set; AddressSanitizer and UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer pass where available. The warning set and the `sanitizers` job are described in @ref Foundation_Workflows_ContinuousIntegration. All seven native jobs build Debug and Release with warnings as errors, and the three sanitizer jobs pass 162/162 under ASan+UBSan, in [GitHub Actions run 36227132453](https://github.com/ChecheRomo96/Foundation/actions/runs/36227132453). Fixing the first hosted run required removing GCC `-Wshadow` and MSVC C4702 findings. |
 * | TEST-006 | P1 | `DONE` | Finish the coverage workflow | Coverage uses a supported compiler, produces a readable report, records a baseline, and has an agreed 1.x quality threshold; otherwise the public option is removed. The GCC `coverage` job publishes an HTML report and enforces the agreed 1.x threshold of 90% line coverage; baselines are 93.0% lines with GCC ([GitHub Actions run 36227132453](https://github.com/ChecheRomo96/Foundation/actions/runs/36227132453)) and 88.8% with Apple Clang. |
 *
 * @section FoundationReleaseV1M4 M4 - Package and Workflow Hardening
 *
 * | ID | Priority | State | Task | Acceptance criteria / evidence |
 * | -- | -------- | ----- | ---- | ------------------------------ |
 * | PKG-001 | P0 | `DONE` | Add a repository-owned package consumer fixture | `tests/PackageConsumer` is isolated from the source tree, validates umbrella and selective includes, links out-of-line Time symbols through the imported target, and passed a fresh `macos_arm64` export on 2026-09-25. See @ref Foundation_Workflows_PackageConsumer. |
 * | PKG-002 | P0 | `IN PROGRESS` | Validate the feature-option matrix | Default, full, each top-level module disabled, and core-only configurations either pass or fail at configure time with a precise dependency error. `tests/cmake/FeatureMatrix.cmake` builds and tests 14 supported selections (default, full, core-only, each of the seven top-level modules and four optional submodules disabled with its dependents) and verifies the exact configure-time error for the 7 unsupported ones. All 21 cases passed locally on macOS Arm64 on 2026-09-26; the first hosted `feature-matrix` run remains to be recorded. See @ref Foundation_Workflows_Configure. |
 * | PKG-003 | P1 | `TODO` | Harden clean and fresh-state behavior | Release validation cannot accidentally reuse stale tests, examples, metadata, or binaries from an earlier configuration. |
 * | PKG-004 | P0 | `TODO` | Verify artifact identity | Each package contains one Release archive, correct headers/metadata, no Debug import, and the expected compiler/architecture/ABI identity. |
 * | PKG-005 | P1 | `TODO` | Validate Arduino source mode | At least the declared Arduino/AVR board compiles the documented sketches from the source layout; untested cores are not advertised as validated. |
 *
 * @section FoundationReleaseV1M5 M5 - Platform and Hardware Validation
 *
 * | ID | Priority | State | Task | Acceptance criteria / evidence |
 * | -- | -------- | ----- | ---- | ------------------------------ |
 * | VAL-001 | P0 | `IN PROGRESS` | Validate macOS arm64 | On macOS 15.3.2 Arm64 with AppleClang 16.0.0, CMake 4.1.1, and Ninja 1.12.1, clean runs passed 161/161 Debug and 161/161 Release tests plus the 1/1 isolated package consumer. `libFoundation.a` is Arm64, the export contains no Debug artifact, and only `IMPORTED_LOCATION_RELEASE` is present. Examples and launcher acceptance remain. |
 * | VAL-002 | P0 | `TODO` | Validate macOS x64 | Cross-build and inspect x86-64 artifacts; run tests/consumer through Rosetta or on Intel hardware. |
 * | VAL-003 | P0 | `IN PROGRESS` | Validate Windows MSVC x64 | The v1.2.0 hosted job passed non-zero Debug/Release tests, Release export, and the external package consumer. Archive inspection plus examples/launcher acceptance on Windows remain. |
 * | VAL-004 | P0 | `IN PROGRESS` | Validate Windows Clang x64 | The v1.2.0 hosted Clang job passed the same tests, export, and consumer. Archive inspection plus examples/launcher acceptance on Windows remain. |
 * | VAL-005 | P0 | `IN PROGRESS` | Validate Linux x64 | GCC and Clang CI jobs completed both configurations, package checks, and consumers for v1.2.0. Local examples/launcher acceptance and a durable evidence record remain. |
 * | VAL-006 | P1 | `IN PROGRESS` | Validate Linux arm64 / Raspberry Pi | Native `ubuntu-24.04-arm` GCC and Clang jobs now run both configurations, export, and package consumers. A green hosted run is required; Raspberry Pi-specific consumer/hardware evidence remains separate. |
 * | VAL-007 | P0 | `IN PROGRESS` | Validate AVR ATmega328P | A clean local AVR-GCC 9.4.0 run built Debug and Release, regenerated the Release-only package, and confirmed `elf32-avr` / `avr:5` members plus `IMPORTED_LOCATION_RELEASE`. Consumer ELF link/size and board or emulator execution remain. |
 * | VAL-008 | P0 | `TODO` | Validate STM32 | All advertised profiles compile and package; at least one real firmware consumer links and executes on representative hardware. |
 * | VAL-009 | P1 | `TODO` | Decide PSoC 5LP status | Exact PSoC toolchain/consumer evidence promotes it to supported; until then it remains experimental. |
 *
 * Store each platform's command log using the record format in
 * @ref FoundationValidationReport. The checklist in
 * @ref Foundation_Workflows_DesktopValidation remains the detailed procedure;
 * this backlog records release status rather than duplicating its commands.
 *
 * @section FoundationReleaseV1M6 M6 - Sustained 1.x Releases
 *
 * | ID | Priority | State | Task | Acceptance criteria / evidence |
 * | -- | -------- | ----- | ---- | ------------------------------ |
 * | REL-001 | P0 | `IN PROGRESS` | Keep release documentation synchronized | README, Doxygen, changelog, support table, license, examples, and package instructions must match the current release and collected evidence. |
 * | REL-002 | P0 | `DEFERRED` | Adopt a release-candidate phase | Versions 1.1.0 and 1.2.0 were published directly from green tagged commits. Use an RC for a future release when compatibility or platform risk justifies it. |
 * | REL-003 | P0 | `DONE` | Run the native release matrix | Native CI and package-consumer validation passed on the exact `v1.2.0` commit in runs 36194411008 and 36194693563. Embedded and hardware evidence remains tracked separately. |
 * | REL-004 | P0 | `DONE` | Publish the current release | @ref Foundation_Workflows_ReleasePackages published five native `v1.2.0` archives and five verified SHA-256 files in [run 36194693563](https://github.com/ChecheRomo96/Foundation/actions/runs/36194693563). |
 * | REL-005 | P0 | `TODO` | Prove downstream readiness | A clean external project consumes the released tag/package without repository-relative paths or unreleased files. |
 *
 * @section FoundationReleaseV1Gates Release Gates
 *
 * Use the gates below before declaring a target `SUPPORTED`, granting external
 * use, or publishing a release whose scope depends on that evidence:
 *
 * - [ ] All P0 tasks are `DONE`; remaining P1 tasks are either `DONE` or
 *       explicitly `DEFERRED` with a documented limitation.
 * - [ ] The support matrix matches collected evidence.
 * - [ ] Required CI is green on the exact release commit.
 * - [ ] Native Debug and Release tests execute and pass; zero tests is rejected.
 * - [ ] Release packages contain no Debug artifacts.
 * - [ ] Separate consumers link the installed packages.
 * - [ ] Required embedded archive, firmware-link, and hardware evidence exists.
 * - [ ] Documentation builds and contains no known release contradiction.
 * - [ ] Qualified legal review has approved the final license, copyright
 *       ownership, contribution terms, and intended distribution model.
 * - [ ] The worktree is clean and the release can be reproduced from a clean clone.
 * - [ ] Release notes, packages, and checksums are ready before creating the final tag.
 */
